A||||7||WKDFIRO||Super Duty 4||||4||
Z||000000||WKDFIRO||12-07-2000||05:10 PM||||FIEROSTETZ asked for specs in  "Fiero or MR2" thread. The place to go for info on the SD4 is this site: <A HREF="http://www.homestead.com/fiero2m4/IronDuke.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.homestead.com/fiero2m4/IronDuke.html</A> <BR>The Super Duty dominated most of the racing venues that it entered. I just finished using most of this site for an article on 4 cylinder performance in our newsletter.<P>300 horse from an Iron Duke is down right unrealistic. It is not a performance block. To do so realisticly would cost you twice that of a V6 and fast approching V8 level. This site gives realistic expectations plus some really awesome specs on the SD4 that almost was - <P>Super Duty 4 cylinder 16 VALVE! <P>It used the SD Block and theoreticly the Iron duke block as well. Pontiac Motorsports put into an 87 SE and called it the Pro Street Formula. Hot Rod did a great article on it. Heres some specs to whet the appetite:<P>- 3.0 l 4 cyl DOHC - 273 hp on Premium gas<BR>- 0-60 - 5.39 seconds<BR>- 1/4 mile (hang on!) 13.37 seconds at 102.11 mph<P>Definitely check that out. <P>As for the reliability of a SD 4 I have never seen an SD4 in a Fiero. Ive seen some built up Iron Dukes (I did some things to my 87 coupe to keep up with the GTs.) but the price of putting a real SD4 in was always more than just putting a V6. Unfortunately the SD4 is just prohibitively expensive to do realisticly. Plus the parts are getting harder to find and more expensive to get them. The V6 (or bigger) is just more rational, proven and cost effective. Would LOVE to hear of someone stepping up for a SD though. FOCOA still had a block last time I saw one.<P>As you read, you might just start getting depressed like I did at the chances that the Fiero had for greatness. Hope it goes for good reading!<p>[This message has been edited by WKDFIRO (edited 12-07-2000).]||||reg||4
Z||000001||FieroSTETZ||12-07-2000||08:07 PM||||im currently saving the cash to buy an sd4- there are a few businesses online that sell them, and i have some connections, i want to get the sd4 and use it as a car for scca competition, i currently have a sponsor- the guy who used to own eagle one before selling it to valvoline- he's a cool guy, and a customer at my compUSA store. he noticed that when i logged in to my computer to perform a data transfer from his, my comp plays an excerpt from my fiero movie and he asked about it, and on and on, so i WILL have a sponsor, and I WANT an sd4- connected to what tranny though, 4.11, getrag, what?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1012904&a=7460599&p=25516673"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Standard||12-08-2000||01:19 AM||||If I ever win the lottery, an SD4 is going to be one of the first things I buy!  More than 300 horsepower from an n/a SD4 is pretty easy.  Just think what you could do with a turbo'd SD4!  &lt;drooool&gt;<P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 153,000 miles and some busted up ground f/x  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/redface.gif"> <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/asthanos.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000003||WKDFIRO||12-08-2000||02:06 AM||||If I were to choose a tranny for autocross I would pick the 85 GT 4 spd Getrag. With the 4.10 I would put in second and third all day long.<P>The site also has some suppliers of SD equipment as well as part numbers. After all these years who knows how accurate they are but at least its a start.<P>Good luck!||||reg||14
Z||000004||Oreif||12-08-2000||02:28 AM||||GM has sold out the design of the SD4.<BR>Go to: <A HREF="http://www.gtsonline.com/krp/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.gtsonline.com/krp/</A> <BR>They have all the SD4 parts. Including using an SD4 block machined to use a chevy V-8 head. (just one   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ) I Emailed them a while back and a 245hp normally asperated SD4 runs about $9800. It is a direct drop in motor for the "Duke".<BR>It is expensive but wouldn't it be interesting to drive one in a Fiero?<P>(click on "Products" and scroll down to "Engine Block")<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 12-08-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||KRMFiero||12-08-2000||08:46 AM||||Cheak out: <A HREF="http://www.flatlanderracing.com/gmpon.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.flatlanderracing.com/gmpon.html</A> <P>They have many parts for the superduty<P>------------------<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE<BR>Front - AudioBahn 4 x 10<BR>Headrest - AudioBahn 3 1/2<P> <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/~Physcokyle/fiero.jpg"> ||||reg||1
